THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

This package bundles no third-party code. Everything it needs at runtime is
supplied by the host:

  flarum/core .......... MIT
      The host application. Declared in composer.json as a requirement, never
      vendored here, and supplied by the forum this extension installs into.

  ext-mbstring, ext-hash, ext-json, ext-curl
      PHP extensions, part of the PHP distribution and licensed under the PHP
      License. Required rather than bundled.

The development requirements -- PHPUnit, and the pinned Infection PHAR the
mutation battery fetches -- are not distributed with this package and do not
appear in an installed extension.

This is why there is no generated THIRD-PARTY.txt beside this file, unlike the
Java artifacts: the generator inventories a resolved dependency graph, and this
package's is empty by construction. If a PHP dependency is ever added, that
stops being true and this file stops being accurate -- ComposerPackageGuardTest
fails if composer.json's `require` grows anything beyond php, ext-*, and
flarum/core.

LICENSE here is byte-identical to the repository's, and a guard asserts it. A
copy that drifts from the licence it claims to be is worse than a reference.
